    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's perfect, exactly what I was looking for. \n\nNow, for the second template, we want to be more strategic with our segmentation. We've noticed that for customers in certain demographics—specifically those from more urban, inner-city areas or lower socioeconomic backgrounds—the formal tone can actually feel a bit cold or even condescending. They tend to respond better to something that feels more \"relatable\" and less \"corporate.\"\n\nCan you draft a second version that's more casual and \"urban-friendly\"? I want it to sound more like how people actually talk in those communities so they feel like the brand actually \"gets\" them. Maybe use some more relaxed language or slang to help build that instant rapport?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
