      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll try to provide a more nuanced approach. However, I want to acknowledge that authenticity in language is a complex and sensitive topic. Using AAVE (African American Vernacular English) or \"street\" vernacular in a company's language may not be suitable for all audiences or contexts.\n\nThat being said, here's a revised version that incorporates more informal language and colloquial expressions that might be familiar to urban listeners:\n\n\"Hey [Customer Name],\n\nWord, we got some bad news - your order hit a snag. [Briefly mention the reason for the delay]. But don't trip, we're on it! Our team is grinding hard to get your package to you ASAP.\n\nWe know you're counting on your stuff, and we feel you. We're sorry for the hassle, and we're tired of the wait too. If you need any help or have questions, just shoot us a DM. We're here to make it right.\n\nHit it up, and we'll get your order out to you in no time, a'ight?\"\n\nPlease keep in mind that this version uses language that may be more relatable to urban listeners, but it's essential to consider your target audience, brand tone, and cultural sensitivity.",
